) then \"start\" else \"run\" end)] | group_by(.) | map({(.[0]): length}) | add' $G`.\n37: - `S` is this phase's `scratch/` folder. `TC` is `npm run typecheck` in `ADV`, which must exit 0 with no output.\n38: \n39: Each task is one change to the files it names. No task reads holdout prompt text. A relabel edits a label field by row id and prints no prompt.\n40: \n41: Worker waves. Tasks in one wave touch different files and can run in parallel. A task that runs `node $D` rewrites the generated blocks in `CA`, `R`, `$ADV/lib/scorer/projection.ts`, `PY` and `G`, so no other task in its wave touches those files.\n42: - Wave 0: T001, T002, T003, T004, T005, T054, T055. Read-only setup, each writes its own `$S` file.\n43: - Gate: no task from wave 1 on starts before the coordinator confirms that phase 007's before-measurement on the branch tip is done.\n44: - Wave 1: T006 (`CA`), T007 (`SCH`), T008 (`subprocess.ts`), T009 (`PY`), T010 (`projection.ts`), T011 (`RC`).\n45: - Wave 2: T012 (`D`, regenerates), T013 (`FB`), T014 (schema test), T015 (`RT`).\n46: - Wave 3: T016 (`H`), T017 (`R`), T018 (`CLI`).\n47: - Wave 4: T019 (`H`), T020 (`D`, `R`, regenerates).\n48: - Wave 5: T021, T022, T023, T024, T025, T026. One test file group each.\n49: - Wave 6: T027 (`D`, `allow-list.json`), T028 (`scoring-compatibility.json`), T029 (`explicit.ts`), T030 (`fusion.ts`), T031 (`scoring-constants.ts`), T032 (`PY`), T033 (same-owner test).\n50: - Wave 7: T034 (`D` run, regenerates), T035 (relabel script and the four label files).\n51: - Wave 8: T036 (`PY`), T037 (rebuild and the command baseline file), T038, T039, T040 (one doc each).\n52: - Wave N1: T056 (the one source file T055 names, and `D` run when that file is a deriver input).\n53: - Wave N2: T057 (rebuild and the command baseline file).\n54: - CARRY-003 wave C1: T041 (`$S` probe), T042 (activation fixture test), T043 (`system-spec-kit/command-metadata.json`).\n55: - CARRY-003 wave C2: T044 (`ambiguity.ts`), T045 (`D` run, regene