{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794529312229,"sessionID":"ses_e2db80168ffeLm0I2SBG3PMsOX","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2483dbd0022TTDktTTG62Eag","sessionID":"ses_e2db80168ffeLm0I2SBG3PMsOX","messageID":"msg_1d24835ea001K5jfqxotorfPYf","type":"tool","id":"call_585d378b901a4721b04cb790","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/tasks.md","offset":120,"limit":30},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/tasks.md, lines 120-149\n120: - [x] T034 Run `node $D`. Verify: `node $D --check | jq -c '{status, counts}'` prints `fresh` with no `allowList` key and `typescriptActive` 45, `jq -c '[.entries[] | .runtime.typescript.id, .runtime.python.id] | map(select(. != null and test(\"^command-spec-kit-(plan|complete|implement|resume)$\")))' $G` prints `[]`, and `$ROLL` prints `{\"ask\":17,\"run\":7,\"start\":20}`.\n121: - [x] T035 [P] Write `$S/relabel-ids.mjs`, which rewrites any JSON string value equal to one of the four old ids to its new id in `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/holdout-prompts.jsonl`, `$ADV/scripts/fixtures/gate2-golden-prompts.jsonl`, `$ADV/scripts/fixtures/skill-advisor-regression-cases.jsonl` and `$ADV/tests/parity/fixtures/local-native-approved-divergences.json`, never prints a prompt and writes file, row id and field per change to `$S/relabel-list.txt`. Run it. Verify: `rg -c \"command-spec-kit-(plan|complete|implement|resume)\\b\"` over the four files prints nothing, and `wc -l < $S/relabel-list.txt` prints 5.\n122: \n123: ### Wave 8\n124: - [x] T036 [P] In `PY`, delete the `\"/prompt\": [(\"sk-prompt\", 3.2)]` lexical row and the `if command == \"/prompt\":` branch of `_command_bridge_owner`. Verify: `rg -n '\"/prompt\"' $PY` prints nothing and `python3 $ADV/tests/python/test_skill_advisor.py` exits 0.\n125: - [x] T037 [P] Run `npm run build` in `ADV`, then `node $C --write`. Verify: `node $C | $M` prints the T001 lines, and `$P` prints `[159,50,20,5]`.\n126: - [x] T038 [P] Describe the head form and the degraded contract in `$HK/skill-advisor-hook.md`. Verify: `rg -n \"→ /speckit:save \\(start\\)|degraded\" $HK/skill-advisor-hook.md` prints at least two lines.\n127: - [x] T039 [P] Describe `kind`, `command`, `policy` and `ownerSkillId` in `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md`. Verify: `rg -c \"ownerSkillId\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md` prints at least 1.\n128: - [x] T040 [P] In `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/README.md`, describe the `GENERATED COMMAND ROWS` block and remove the allow-list as a live source. Verify: `rg -n \"COMMAND_ROWS\" $ADV/scripts/command-bridges/README.md` prints a line and `rg -n \"allow-list.json\" $ADV/scripts/command-bridges/README.md` prints nothing.\n129: \n130: ### Wave N1\n131: - [ ] T056 Make one correction at the source T055 names: remove a token a skill holds only through a harvest artifact, or add a general documentation-edit term to the `sk-doc` source field T055 names. The change adds no string of two or more consecutive words from the `nm-sk-doc-01` prompt. When the file is a deriver input, run `node $D`. Verify: for each two-word window of the prompt, `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff HEAD -U0 -- <changed file> | rg -F \"<window>\"` prints nothing, `node $D --check | jq -r .status` prints `fresh`, and after `npm run build` in `ADV`, `node $S/nm-sk-doc-probe.mjs` prints `sk-doc` with the highest score.\n132: \n133: ### Wave N2\n134: - [ ] T057 Run `npm run build` in `ADV`, then `node $C --write`. Verify: `jq -c '.rows[\"nm-sk-doc-01\"] | {top, offered}' $ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json` prints `{\"top\":\"sk-doc\",\"offered\":false}`, `node $C | $M` prints typed at least 24 of 44, tune combined at least 9 of 45, holdout combined at least 0 of 44 and false offers 0 of 35, and `$P` prints numbers no lower than `[159,50,20]` with false fire no higher than 5. If any is worse, revert T056 and mark it `[B]` with the printed numbers.\n135: \n136: ### CARRY-003 wave C1\n137: - [ ] T041 [P] CARRY-003 (a): write `$S/agent-ambiguity.mjs`, which sets `VITEST`, imports `scoreAdvisorPrompt` from `$ADV/dist/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.js` and prints `ambiguous` and, for the top four rows, `skill`, `confidence`, `score`, `confidenceFloored` and the length of `ambiguousWith`, for `/create:agent dependency-auditor for release checks`. Save the output (`$S/agent-ambiguity.txt`). Verify: the output shows the top row `create:agent` with `confidenceFloored` true clustered with floored rows. If it shows a different cause, mark T044 `[B]` with that cause.\n138: - [ ] T042 [P] CARRY-003 (b): in `$ADV/tests/command-policy-derivation.vitest.ts`, add a case that builds a fixture skills root through the file's existing fixture seam with one standalone skill whose `command-metadata.json` declares a command that `scoring-compatibility.json` does not list, and asserts the derived entry is enabled for both `typescript` and `python`. Verify: in `ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/command-policy-derivation.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n139: - [ ] T043 [P] CARRY-003 (c): add `which packets mention` to `userIntent.ownedSignals` of `/speckit:search` in `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/command-metadata.json`. Verify: `jq -c '.[] | select(.command == \"/speckit:search\") | .userIntent.ownedSignals | index(\"which packets mention\")' .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/command-metadata.json` prints a number.\n140: \n141: ### CARRY-003 wave C2\n142: - [ ] T044 CARRY-003 (a): in `clustersWithTop` (`$ADV/lib/scorer/ambiguity.ts`), when both the top and the member carry `confidenceFloored`, cluster on the score margin alone. Verify: in `ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/scorer` reports 0 failed and `$P` prints `[159,50,20,5]`. If `$P` moves, revert the change and mark this task `[B]` with the printed numbers.\n143: - [ ] T045 Run `node $D`. Verify: `node $D --check | jq -r .status` prints `fresh`.\n144: \n145: ### CARRY-003 wave C3\n146: - [ ] T046 Run `npm run build` in `ADV`, then `node $C --write`. Verify: `node $C | $M` prints `[]` as its fourth line with the first three lines as in T001, `$P` prints `[159,50,20,5]`, and `$REC '{\"prompt\":\"show me which packets mention the token cap\"}' | jq -c '[.data.recommendations[] | select(.command == \"/speckit:search\") | .policy]'` prints `[\"run\"]`.\n147: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n148: \n149: ---\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 150]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/tasks.md, lines 120-149\n120: - [x] T034 Run `node $D`. Verify: `node $D --check | jq -c '{status, counts}'` prints `fresh` with no `allowList` key and `typescriptActive` 45, `jq -c '[.entries[] | .runtime.typescript.id, .runtime.python.id] | map(select(. != null and test(\"^command-spec-kit-(plan|complete|implement|resume)$\")))' $G` prints `[]`, and `$ROLL` prints `{\"ask\":17,\"run\":7,\"start\":20}`.\n121: - [x] T035 [P] Write `$S/relabel-ids.mjs`, which rewrites any JSON string value equal to one of the four old ids to its new id in `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/holdout-prompts.jsonl`, `$ADV/scripts/fixtures/gate2-golden-prompts.jsonl`, `$ADV/scripts/fixtures/skill-advisor-regression-cases.jsonl` and `$ADV/tests/parity/fixtures/local-native-approved-divergences.json`, never prints a prompt and writes file, row id and field per change to `$S/relabel-list.txt`. Run it. Verify: `rg -c \"command-spec-kit-(plan|complete|implement|resume)\\b\"` over the four files prints nothing, and `wc -l < $S/relabel-list.txt` prints 5.\n122: \n123: ### Wave 8\n124: - [x] T036 [P] In `PY`, delete the `\"/prompt\": [(\"sk-pro