ib/scorer/ambiguity.ts`), when both the top and the member carry `confidenceFloored`, cluster on the score margin alone. Verify: in `ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/scorer` reports 0 failed and `$P` prints `[159,50,20,5]`. If `$P` moves, revert the change and mark this task `[B]` with the printed numbers.\n143: - [ ] T045 Run `node $D`. Verify: `node $D --check | jq -r .status` prints `fresh`.\n144: \n145: ### CARRY-003 wave C3\n146: - [ ] T046 Run `npm run build` in `ADV`, then `node $C --write`. Verify: `node $C | $M` prints `[]` as its fourth line with the first three lines as in T001, `$P` prints `[159,50,20,5]`, and `$REC '{\"prompt\":\"show me which packets mention the token cap\"}' | jq -c '[.data.recommendations[] | select(.command == \"/speckit:search\") | .policy]'` prints `[\"run\"]`.\n147: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n148: \n149: ---\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 150]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/tasks.md\",\"offset\":120,\"limit\":30}"},"time":{"start":1794529312189,"end":1794529312229}}}}
