{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794529320520,"sessionID":"ses_e2db80168ffeLm0I2SBG3PMsOX","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2485cc0001qk94wmYOZG6Ef8","sessionID":"ses_e2db80168ffeLm0I2SBG3PMsOX","messageID":"msg_1d2485732001I5rTyIJKqK7x5U","type":"tool","id":"call_3bcd8d8778dd4ca0b6725e66","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/scratch/nm-sk-doc-source.txt"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/scratch/nm-sk-doc-source.txt, lines 1-26\n1: # nm-sk-doc-01 token source trace\n2: \n3: Date: 2026-11-12\n4: Input: scratch/nm-sk-doc-before.txt, probe prompt \"fix the typo in the heading of the setup guide\"\n5: Code read: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/lexical.ts` and `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/projection.ts`\n6: \n7: ## How a skill's token list is built\n8: \n9: `scoreLexicalLane` builds each skill's candidate strings from `id`, `name`, `description`, `domains`, `intentSignals` and `keywords`. It scores them with `scoreTokenOverlap` and harvests `token:<x>` evidence with a plain `haystack.includes(token)` over the same joined candidates.\n10: `projectionFromRow` fills `name`, `description` and `keywords` from the skill's `SKILL.md` through `parseSkillMarkdown`, and `domains` and `intentSignals` from the `skill_nodes` row. `indexSkillMetadata` reads that row from the skill's `graph-metadata.json` fields `domains` and `intent_signals`, so an edit to `graph-metadata.json` reaches the SQLite projection only after a re-index.\n11: \n12: ## Token sources\n13: \n14: typo | sk-code | .skilled/skills/sk-code/graph-metadata.json | field domains | \"typography\" gives token:typo by substring only, while scoreTokenOverlap tokenizes and does not score typo against typography\n15: heading | sk-code | .skilled/skills/sk-code/graph-metadata.json | field intent_signals | \"text-wrap balance headings\" gives token:heading by substring and scores 0.45 through the heading to headings suffix extension\n16: guide | sk-design | .skilled/skills/sk-design/graph-metadata.json | field intent_signals | \"style guide from\" and \"style guide from a url\" give token:guide as an exact token\n17: setup | system-skilled-doctor | .skilled/skills/system-skilled-doctor/graph-metadata.json | field intent_signals | \"doctor setup\", \"doctor setup diagnostic\" and \"what doctor setup prints\" give token:setup. The separate derived:setup evidence comes from field derived.key_files, \".skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md\" reduced to \"setup\"\n18: debug | sk-code | .skilled/skills/sk-code/SKILL.md | field description | \"Implement, debug and verify code...\" gives token:debug as an exact token. The same token is also in the SKILL.md Keywords block and in graph-metadata.json intent_signals \"debug the ci\"\n19: \n20: ## Why sk-doc holds no documentation-edit token\n21: \n22: `sk-doc` projects documentation artifacts and authoring actions (`documentation`, `markdown`, `authoring`, `readme`, `feature catalog`, `frontmatter`, `create`, `validate`, `review the docs`) but no term for editing existing prose, such as typo, heading, spelling, proofread or wording. The prompt's scorable tokens are `fix`, `typo`, `heading`, `setup` and `guide`, plus the synonyms `debug`, `correct` and `patch` that `fix` injects. None is a whole token in `sk-doc`'s candidate strings. The only literal \"fix\" sits inside \"fixture\" in `intent_signals` (\"benchmark fixture\" and \"reviewer-prompt fixture\"). Scoring is whole-token, so the 3-letter prompt token `fix` does not match `fixture`, `sk-doc` scores 0, and `scoreLexicalLane` drops a row at score <= 0.05 before it can harvest evidence. That is why `sk-doc` carries no token and never enters the recommendation list.\n23: \n24: ## sk-doc source field that should carry documentation-edit vocabulary\n25: \n26: sk-doc source field: .skilled/skills/sk-doc/graph-metadata.json -> intent_signals","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/scratch/nm-sk-doc-source.txt, lines 1-26\n1: # nm-sk-doc-01 token source trace\n2: \n3: Date: 2026-11-12\n4: Input: scratch/nm-sk-doc-before.txt, probe prompt \"fix the typo in the heading of the setup guide\"\n5: Code read: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/lexical.ts` and `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/projection.ts`\n6: \n7: ## How a skill's token list is built\n8: \n9: `scoreLexicalLane` builds each skill's candidate strings from `id`, `name`, `description`, `domains`, `intentSignals` and `keywords`. It scores them with `scoreTokenOverlap` and harvests `token:<x>` evidence with a plain `haystack.includes(token)` over the same joined candidates.\n10: `projectionFromRow` fills `name`, `description` and `keywords` from the skill's `SKILL.md` through `parseSkillMarkdown`, and `domains` and `intentSignals` from the `skill_nodes` row. `indexSkillMetadata` reads that row from the skill's `graph-metadata.json` fields `domains` and `intent_signals`, so an edit to `graph-metadata.json` reaches the SQLite projection only after a re-index.\n11: \n12: ## Token sources\n13: \n14: typo | sk-code | .skilled/skills/sk-code/graph-metadata.json | field domains | \"typography\" gives token:typo by substring only, while scoreTokenOverlap tokenizes and does not score typo against typography\n15: heading | sk-code | .skilled/skills/sk-code/graph-metadata.json | field intent_signals | \"text-wrap balance headings\" gives token:heading by substring and scores 0.45 through the heading to headings suffix extension\n16: guide | sk-design | .skilled/skills/sk-design/graph-metadata.json | field intent_signals | \"style guide from\" and \"style guide from a url\" give token:guide as an exact token\n17: setup | system-skilled-doctor | .skilled/skills/system-skilled-doctor/graph-metadata.json | field intent_signals | \"doctor setup\", \"doctor setup diagnostic\" and \"what doctor setup prints\" give token:setup. The separate derived:setup evidence comes from field derived.key_files, \".skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md\" reduced to \"setup\"\n18: debug | sk-code | .skilled/skills/sk-code/SKILL.md | field description | \"Implement, debug and verify code...\" gives token:debug as an exact token. The same token is also in the SKILL.md Keywords block and in graph-metadata.json intent_signals \"debug the ci\"\n19: \n20: ## Why sk-doc holds no documentation-edit token\n21: \n22: `sk-doc` projects documentation artifacts and authoring actions (`documentation`, `markdown`, `authoring`, `readme`, `feature catalog`, `frontmatter`, `create`, `validate`, `review the docs`) but no term for editing existing prose, such as typo, heading, spelling, proofread or wording. The prompt's scorable tokens are `fix`, `typo`, `heading`, `setup` and `guide`, plus the synonyms `debug`, `correct` and `patch` that `fix` injects. None is a whole token in `sk-doc`'s candidate strings. The only literal \"fix\" sits inside \"fixture\" in `intent_signals` (\"benchmark fixture\" and \"reviewer-prompt fixture\"). Scoring is whole-token, so the 3-letter prompt token `fix` does not match `fixture`, `sk-doc` scores 0, and `scoreLexicalLane` drops a row at score <= 0.05 before it can harvest evidence. That is why `sk-doc` carries no token and never enters the recommendation list.\n23: \n24: ## sk-doc source field that should carry documentation-edit vocabulary\n25: \n26: sk-doc source field: .skilled/skills/sk-doc/graph-metadata.json -> intent_signals"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/scratch/nm-sk-doc-source.txt\"}"},"time":{"start":1794529320128,"end":1794529320520}}}}
