{"type":"text","timestamp":1794529771949,"sessionID":"ses_e2db80168ffeLm0I2SBG3PMsOX","part":{"id":"prt_1d24f301d001Qa8pngiKkCL6I1","sessionID":"ses_e2db80168ffeLm0I2SBG3PMsOX","messageID":"msg_1d24f092c001nTdRVotW4KScDT","type":"text","text":"Done. T056 made one correction at the source T055 named.\n\n**File written**\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/graph-metadata.json` — added one entry to `intent_signals`: `\"typo, spelling, heading and wording edits to a guide\"` (line 308). `intent_signals_generated` is untouched. No other file changed by me.\n\n**Why this entry**\n`sk-doc` held documentation-authoring vocabulary but no documentation-edit vocabulary. T055 named `graph-metadata.json -> intent_signals`; the added vocabulary covers the edit classes T055 listed (typo, spelling, heading, wording) applied to a guide, without containing any two-word window of the `nm-sk-doc-01` prompt.\n\n**Verify output**\n\nTwo-word windows of the prompt against `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff HEAD -U0 -- .skilled/skills/sk-doc/graph-metadata.json`:\n```\nfix the -> 0\nthe typo -> 0\ntypo in -> 0\nin the -> 0\nthe heading -> 0\nheading of -> 0\nof the -> 0\nthe setup -> 0\nsetup guide -> 0\n```\n(0 matching lines each)\n\n`node $D --check | jq -r .status`:\n```\nfresh\n```\n\n`npm run build` in ADV: `build_exit=0`\n\n`node $S/nm-sk-doc-probe.mjs`:\n```\nsk-doc 0.82 0.1920 [[\"lexical\",0.168,[\"token:fix\",\"token:typo\",\"token:heading\",\"token:guide\"]],[\"semantic_shadow\",0.024,[\"shadow:test-fallback\"]]]\nsystem-skilled-doctor 0.82 0.1301 [[\"lexical\",0.056,[\"token:setup\"]],[\"derived_generated\",0.0661,[\"derived:setup\"]],[\"semantic_shadow\",0.008,[\"shadow:test-fallback\"]]]\nsk-code 0.82 0.0969 [[\"lexical\",0.0812,[\"token:typo\",\"token:heading\",\"token:debug\"]],[\"graph_causal\",0.0157,[\"edge:mcp-tooling->sk-code:enhances\",\"edge:sk-design->sk-code:enhances\"]]]\nsk-design 0.82 0.0640 [[\"lexical\",0.056,[\"token:guide\"]],[\"semantic_shadow\",0.008,[\"shadow:test-fallback\"]]]\ncount 5 skdoc index 0\n```\n\n`sk-doc` is first with the highest score (0.1920). I did not run bare `node $D` because `graph-metadata.json` is not a deriver input (the deriver reads command metadata and skill directory names only), and `--check` confirms the generated surfaces are fresh. Checkbox in `tasks.md` left unticked.","time":{"start":1794529767453,"end":1794529771949}}}
